#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087496 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ba25c0c-9ba9-586a-b66f-7f07076d2827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Exponential Growth Problem"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ec4eaee-0872-55a3-abef-1b66f9d43969" :question/math-academy-id "e-542" :question/problem "Suppose that the population $P(t)$ of a town after $t$ years can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}P} {\\textrm{d}t} = 0.02P$.\n\nIf there are currently $500$ people in the town, what will be the town's population in $3$ years?" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We note that this is an exponential growth differential equation with $r = 0.02$. Therefore, the solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t) = P_0\\,e^{0.02t}\n$$\n\nwhere $P_0$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that the population is currently $500$, so we have $P_0 = 500$.\n\nTherefore, the population of the town at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nP(t) = 500\\,e^{0.02t}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the population after $3$ years, we substitute $t=3$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(3) &= 500e^{0.02 \\cdot 3} \\\\\n&= 500e^{0.06} \\\\\n&\\approx 531\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the population will be approximately $531$ after $3$ years."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087561 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a63a0ae-3e16-5cdb-92f5-fea09351db84" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Unknown Rate"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9e8b643-2650-5481-9210-46e796417449" :question/math-academy-id "e-7273" :question/problem "The number of followers of a celebrity's social media account increases at a rate that is directly proportional to the number of followers at that time. Given that there are currently $600\\,000$ followers and in $3$ months there will be $780\\,000$ followers, what is the growth rate? Round your answer to the nearest percent." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The rate $N'(t)$ at which the number of followers increases is directly proportional to the number of followers $N$. Therefore, we can model the number of followers using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d} N}{\\mathrm{d} t} = rN\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is measured in months, and $r > 0$ is the growth rate.\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nN(t) = N_0\\,e^{rt}\n$$\n\nwhere $N_0$ is the initial number of followers.\n\nWe're told that there are currently $600\\,000$ followers, so we have\n\n$$\nN_0 = 600\\,000\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number of followers $N$ after $t$ months is\n\n$$\nN(t) = 600\\,000 \\, e^{rt}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the growth rate, we substitute\n\n$$\nN(3)=780\\,000\n$$\n\ninto the equation above and solve for $r$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(3) &= 600000e^{r \\cdot 3} \\\\\n780000 &= 600000e^{3r} \\\\\ne^{3r} &= \\frac{780000}{600000} \\\\\ne^{3r} &= 1.3 \\\\\n\\ln (e^{3r}) &= \\ln (1.3) \\\\\n3r &= \\ln (1.3) \\\\\nr &= \\frac{1}{3}\\ln (1.3) \\\\\n&\\approx 0.087455\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nr\\approx 9\\%\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest percent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087562 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6330530-50c5-51e9-b616-2b97ce42cade" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Exponential Decay Problem"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "770866d5-545f-5ab7-a48e-df9ca76f248e" :question/math-academy-id "e-7312" :question/problem "Suppose that the value $V(t)$ of a particular car can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t} = -0.1V$,\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the car was first purchased. If the car was purchased for $10000$ dollars, what will it be worth after $3$ years?" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the right-hand side of the equation is *negative*, which means that the car's value is *decreasing.*\n\nThis is an exponential decay differential equation with $r = 0.1$. Therefore, the general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nV(t) = V_0 e^{-0.1 t}\n$$\n\nWe know that the car was first purchased for $10000$ dollars. Therefore,\n\n$$\nV_0 = 10\\,000\n$$\n\nand we have the particular solution\n\n$$\nV(t) = 10\\,000 e^{-0.1 t}\n$$\n\nTo find the car's value after $3$ years, we substitute $t=3$ into the particular solution above. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV(3) &= 10000e^{-0.1 \\cdot 3} \\\\\n&= 10000e^{-0.3} \\\\\n&\\approx 7408\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the car will be worth approximately $7408$ dollars after three years."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6330530-50c5-51e9-b616-2b97ce42cade" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Exponential Decay Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00962f1f-db2c-59bc-9f7e-5fe54dafb7fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "206" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084742} {:answer/id #uuid "307ecbcb-812b-5092-b9be-73e4c83df8a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084743} {:answer/id #uuid "3981cd65-9e1c-563f-be6c-f4ce96fb507b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084744} {:answer/id #uuid "41dd311a-9125-53c2-a975-2c507f3e0c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "403" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084745} {:answer/id #uuid "42d8b6f4-bb9d-59aa-9ee2-ecd8a9fbb5ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3981cd65-9e1c-563f-be6c-f4ce96fb507b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084744} :answer-field/id #uuid "2242460b-abaa-510f-8979-8aff219860ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "884109e1-5e14-5c1c-933b-9800a24392f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-15208" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nThe number of particles $N(t)$ in a radioactive substance after $t$ years can be modeled by the differential equation\n$\\frac{dN}{dt} =-3N$.\nIf there were $8500$ particles initially, calculate the number of particles remaining after $2$ years. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The solution of $N^{\\prime}=-3N$ is $N(t)=Ce^{-3t}$. Since $N(0)=8500$, we obtain $N(2)=8500e^{-6}\\approx21.069$. There are $21$ particles remaining to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6330530-50c5-51e9-b616-2b97ce42cade" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Exponential Decay Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3b1ce06-482a-55fe-b920-64490e6d5988" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$966$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087079} {:answer/id #uuid "eaec3854-187a-51e6-a9f8-0e6929a4a4d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$586$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087080} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f1627c-dcc7-5721-b79e-708add217115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$125$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087081} {:answer/id #uuid "64d05707-47c1-526b-bc59-a2f9885154f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$355$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087082} {:answer/id #uuid "6f99f62e-6333-5466-a5d4-d5ab69c16ce9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$216$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eaec3854-187a-51e6-a9f8-0e6929a4a4d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$586$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087080} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffbb2fad-1e3c-58c3-a10d-0dff2ab6a47f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6894d124-282d-5217-8531-e4a1976ca68b" :question/math-academy-id "q-83140" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nThe outstanding amount $L(t)$ that Daphne needs to repay the bank $t$ years after taking out a loan can be modeled by the differential equation\n$\\frac{dL}{dt} =-0.5L$.\n\nIf she borrowed $32000$ dollars, calculate the debt remaining after $8$ years. Round your answer to the nearest dollar." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The solution of $L^{\\prime}=-0.5L$ is $L(t)=Ce^{-0.5t}$. The initial debt gives $C=32000$, so $L(8)=32000e^{-4}\\approx586.100$. The remaining debt is $586$ dollars to the nearest dollar."}]}
